    {
      "id": 158343,
      "name": "Blossercubbles",
      "username": "Blossercubbles",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/blossercubbles/{size}/1863_2.png",
      "created_at": "2016-02-07T15:13:04.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I agree on the Freedom Six unlocks. Going through each unlock with my fiance, some are just so convoluted that it never feels like playing. The conditions aren't something that would organically happen most of the time, so the whole game is just manipulating one hero with various powers, heaps of friendly fire, and mountains of waiting (I'm looking at Dark Watch NightMist here. Or Horus Ra.) It's still a slight sense of accomplishment when that variant pops up, but I sure am sick of Ambuscade and GloomWeaver, just to have the benefit of not having things destroyed before the other seventeen parts of the puzzle fall into place.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I did have some legitimate fun unlocking Price of Freedom Wraith, however! It basically felt like playing a regular game, just with a layer of a challenge, instead of half a dozen unnecessary-but-neat-story-wise hoops. Also, that was actually the first time I brought Mr Fixer against his nemeses. It was fantastic.</p>",
      "post_number": 7,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:38:26.617Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
